// ClientHellos captured from a real client, for the tests of the ClientHello
// reader (client_hello_test.mbt). The client is `openssl s_client` of
// OpenSSL 4.1.0 (23 Oct 2026), on linux-aarch64. Each capture is every octet
// the client sent before it waited for the server: one TLS record that holds
// its ClientHello. A listener on the loopback interface wrote what it received
// to a file, and closed the connection after one idle second (socat 1.8.1.3):
//
//   socat -T 1 -u TCP-LISTEN:47289,bind=127.0.0.1,reuseaddr CREATE:tls13-sni.bin &
//   openssl s_client -connect 127.0.0.1:47289 -servername users.example.test -alpn h2,http/1.1 -trace </dev/null
//
// The other two ran the same way, with the options their comments give.
// `-trace` printed OpenSSL's own decoding of the ClientHello it sent; the
// layout given for each capture is from it. No certificate is involved: the
// listener never answered. The names asked for are Hosts of the kind a Mock
// with its own certificate has (docs/running.md, "Certificates for single
// Mocks"), under the `.test` name that RFC 6761 reserves for tests. The
// random, the session ID and the key shares are the client's random values of
// that run, and its private keys were never kept.
//
// The layouts give each length field as an octet offset in the handshake
// message, the capture after its 5-octet record header (RFC 8446, section
// 5.1), whose handshake header takes 4 octets (section 4). The ClientHello's
// body starts at offset 4 (section 4.1.2).

///|
/// The octets of a capture, from its hex.
fn captured(hex : String) -> Bytes {
  @hex.decode(hex.replace_all(old="\n", new="")) catch {
    _ => abort("a capture is hex")
  }
}

///|
/// A TLS 1.3 ClientHello that asks for `users.example.test`, and offers `h2`
/// and `http/1.1` by ALPN, as an HTTP/2 client does:
/// `openssl s_client -servername users.example.test -alpn h2,http/1.1`.
/// 1,610 octets: a record of 1,605, a ClientHello of 1,601.
///
/// Layout, by message offset: legacy_session_id length 32 at 38; cipher_suites
/// length 60 at 71; compression_methods length 1 at 133; extensions length
/// 1,468 at 135. Thirteen extensions follow, from 137 to the end at 1,605:
/// key_share's type at 287 and its length, 1,258, at 289; server_name's type
/// at 1,560, its length, 23, at 1,562, the server_name_list length, 21, at
/// 1,564, the name type, 0 (host_name), at 1,566, the HostName length, 18, at
/// 1,567 and `users.example.test` from 1,569; then ALPN's extension, the
